Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.77,0:02:49.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am,\Nhow ya doin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.47,0:02:51.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this Rose Hill?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.84,0:02:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Good,\NThis is Ed Couch.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.48,0:02:56.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Vesta Adcock's nephew.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.98,0:02:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to get up there\Nand see her,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.28,0:03:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'm gonna be late\N'cause I'm lost out here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.35,0:03:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We're off the Alabama interstate\Nbut I don't know where.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.26,0:03:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did you hear that?\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.23,0:03:48.30,Default,,0,0,0,,The train.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.36,0:03:51.24,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I didn't hear\Nno train.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.00,0:03:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, nothin',\NI guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.40,0:03:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where's "Whistle Stop"\Non the map?\N- I can't find it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.87,0:04:03.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did you tell me to\Nturn right 10 miles back there?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.28,0:04:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,God, you got a negative\Nsense of direction, hon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.88,0:04:11.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.82,0:04:16.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Ed,your aunt's gonna be\Nso disappointed we're late.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.09,0:04:20.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I know she's\Nbeen looking forward to\Nthis visit all week long.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.16,0:04:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Bless her sweet,\Nlittle ol' heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.57,0:04:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, how's my sweet Auntie V\Nthis afternoon?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.50,0:04:33.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember us?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.17,0:04:36.24,Default,,0,0,0,,- Don't you look pretty!\N- We brought you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.31,0:04:39.48,Default,,0,0,0,,- Let me look at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.55,0:04:42.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you know\NEvelyn loves you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.22,0:04:47.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, honey,\NI guess it'd be better if\Nyou wait out here for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.12,0:04:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,-I'll get all this stuff.\N- Well, if you think it's best.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.66,0:04:54.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I do this time.\NOkay?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.03,0:04:57.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Have a nice day,\NAunt Vesta.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.27,0:04:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you pitch a fit\Nlike that'
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.18,0:05:13.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you know\Nthey took my gallbladder out?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.32,0:05:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.52,0:05:21.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes. Still\Nin the hospital in ajar.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.26,0:05:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess that's where\Nthey keep 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.13,0:05:28.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.16,0:05:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,When I was\Nin the hospital,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.46,0:05:34.43,Default,,0,0,0,,the nurse gave me one of them\NFleet enemas they're so fond of.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.50,0:05:37.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Cleo Threadgoode,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.17,0:05:40.48,Default,,0,0,0,,82 year old widow,\Nimagine that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.54,0:05:43.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually,\Neverybody calls me Ninny.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.74,0:05:45.98,Default,,0,0,0,,'Course I'm\Njust visitin' here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.05,0:05:51.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you ever have\None of them Fleet enemas?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.39,0:05:53.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Um,well?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.39,0:05:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.52,0:05:58.76,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd remember it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.83,0:06:02.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Me and my friend, Mrs. Otis,\Ncome from Whistle Stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.56,0:06:04.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You ever been\Nto Whistle Stop?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.83,0:06:08.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, yes. I just\Npassed by there today.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.30,0:06:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,She's lived\Ndown the street from me\Nfor 30 years or more.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.24,0:06:15.24,Default,,0,0,0,,After her son died,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.31,0:06:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,her daughter-in-law had a fit\Nfor her to come live\Nat the nursing home.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.98,0:06:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,They asked me to come\Nand be her roommate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.35,0:06:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Otis don't know it,\Nbut I'm going home just soon\Nas she gets settled in good.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.92,0:06:32.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Does the name\N"Idgie Threadgoode"\Nring a bell?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.39,0:06:35.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, no, ma'am.\NI don't think so.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.00,0:06:38.81,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd remember her.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.87,0:06:42.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You see,\NI was practically adopted\Nby the Threadgoode family.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.84,0:06:45.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- I married her brother, Cleo.\N- Oh, uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.22,0:06:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, now, let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.92,0:06:56.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I 'member the day they pulled\Nthat truck up out of the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.78,0:07:07.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I 'member the day we\Nwas all gettin' ready\Nfor Leona's weddin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.62,0:07:09.60,Default,,0,0,0,,The war had just ended,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.66,0:07:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,the Great one,\Nyou know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.06,0:07:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,And another one\Nwas about to begin in\Nthe Threadgoode house.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.80,0:07:19.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Sipsey hone )4\Nis that finished?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.80,0:07:23.75,Default,,0,0,0,,- Buddy,\Nget dressed honey.\N- Mama?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.80,0:07:25.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Leona, what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.84,0:07:27.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie's upstairs\Nin her room...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.77,0:07:29.75,Default,,0,0,0,,and says she won't come out\Nas long as she lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.81,0:07:31.95,Default,,0,0,0,,- She is gonna ruin my weddin'!\N- Shh.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.01,0:07:34.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Leona, you're gonna be\Nthe most beautiful bride.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.88,0:07:38.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course she is, Papa.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.22,0:07:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Your papa has spent\Nevery last nickel he has\Njust to make you happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.22,0:07:46.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, you try to act\Na little grateful, young lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.09,0:07:49.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Imogene Louise Threadgoode!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.26,0:07:51.80,Default,,0,0,0,,This is your mama!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.20,0:07:59.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You come down here right now.\NDo you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.21,0:08:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,- Buddy, fetch her.\NShe'll listen to you.\N- Come on down, little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.91,0:08:04.48,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no firin'\Nsquad waitin' for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.54,0:08:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Ohh! Come on, honey\NLet us see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.95,0:08:12.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You look so pretty.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.19,0:08:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,- I see London,\NI see-\N- Hush!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.76,0:08:20.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Julian, hush.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.26,0:08:23.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Come ahead, sweetheart.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.06,0:08:26.80,Default,,0,0,0,,You look awful nice\Nin that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.87,0:08:28.47,Default,,0,0,0,,- Mama!\N- You look fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.53,0:08:31.03,Default,,0,0,0,,She looks like a monkey
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.10,0:08:32.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Julian, stop it\Nright this second!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.97,0:08:36.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Take it back!\NTake it back!\NIdgie, hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.38,0:08:39.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you she\Nwas gonna ruin my weddin'!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.55,0:08:41.93,Default,,0,0,0,,- Idgie, get up.\N- Take it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.98,0:08:44.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Take it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.22,0:08:47.57,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'll get you for this.\N- No, Buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.36,0:08:54.43,Default,,0,0,0,,We have to be careful\Nwhen she's dressing up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.49,0:08:56.44,Default,,0,0,0,,She's just a pain!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.50,0:09:00.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Leona, will you\Nstop shrieking'
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.10,0:09:02.81,Default,,0,0,0,,This is your\Nweddin ' day'
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.81,0:09:16.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I oaks like you got yourself\Nup a tree, little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.72,0:09:19.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sick of people\Nmakin' fun of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.82,0:09:22.36,Default,,0,0,0,,So you're gonna stay up here\Nall day long.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.42,0:09:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep.\NThe hell with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.69,0:09:29.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Who wants to wear\Nthat stupid ol' dress anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.70,0:09:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,- I ever tell you about the oysters?\N- Oysters?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.13,0:09:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,- I tell you about the oysters?\N- No.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.13,0:09:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Think about the millions of\Noysters lyin' around the ocean.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.87,0:09:42.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Then one day...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.28,0:09:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,God comes along and sees one\Nand he says,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.14,0:09:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,"I think I'm gonna make\Nthat one different."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.11,0:09:50.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what he does?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.38,0:09:53.55,Default,,0,0,0,,He puts a little\Npiece of sand in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.62,0:09:57.86,Default,,0,0,0,,- Guess what it can do\Nthat the others can't.\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.92,0:10:01.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It can make\Na beautiful pearl.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.29,0:10:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,What if God\Nmade a mistake?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.53,0:10:08.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the way I figure it,\Nhe never makes mistakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.70,0:10:11.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, he made sure\Nwe got together.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.54,0:10:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,He made sure you got\Nthe best looking,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.61,0:10:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,most charmin' brother\Nin the world...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.88,0:10:19.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- who's gonna beat you\Nto the chocolate cake.\N- You will not.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.31,0:10:21.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Got you out of the tree,\Ndidn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.75,0:10:24.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Did not!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.75,0:10:28.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Into this estate,\Nthese two come now to be joined
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.45,0:10:30.56,Default,,0,0,0,,If any man present\Ncan show cause...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.62,0:10:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,why they may not lawfully\Nbe joined together,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.09,0:10:38.23,Default,,0,0,0,,let him speak now or\Nforever after hold his peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.30,0:10:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Please be seated.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.34,0:10:45.55,Default,,0,0,0,,If either of you\Nknow any reason...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.61,0:10:48.59,Default,,0,0,0,,why you may not justly\Nbe joined together\Nin holy matrimony
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.64,0:10:51.12,Default,,0,0,0,,do you now confess it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.75,0:11:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,It is then your will\Nto proceed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.52,0:11:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you,\NCharles Osgood justice-
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.07,0:11:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you. I don't know what\Nwe'd do without your generosity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.47,0:11:19.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Sipsey, especially you.\NLook what you've clone!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.51,0:11:23.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Mrs. Threadgoode.\NGimme that, you rascal!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.78,0:11:30.35,Default,,0,0,0,,John!\NJump on my back
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.42,0:11:34.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think\Nthere ever was a sweeter boy\Nthan Buddy Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.12,0:11:38.63,Default,,0,0,0,,- You look beautiful, Lily.\N- Yes, Lily, you sure do.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.69,0:11:42.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I had the biggest crush\Non him.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.19,0:11:44.53,Default,,0,0,0,,He was a terrible flirt!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.60,0:11:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,But his heart belonged\Nto Ruth Jamison.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.90,0:11:51.07,Default,,0,0,0,,She was the daughter of\Na friend of his mama's...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.14,0:11:53.95,Default,,0,0,0,,who was visitin'\Nthat summer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.01,0:11:57.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth Jamison,\Nyou're just the one\NI've been lookin' for.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.54,0:12:00.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you thirsty?\N- Let's go visit\Nsomeplace else.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.55,0:12:09.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Think that's a big lake,\Nyou should've seen the\None next to our house.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.96,0:12:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,We used to swim in it\Nand fish.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.16,0:12:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I sure do miss it.\NSure do.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.89,0:12:17.63,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to it?\NDid it dry up?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.70,0:12:19.65,Default,,0,0,0,,No, worse than that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.70,0:12:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Last fall,\Na ﬂock of ducks,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.83,0:12:26.11,Default,,0,0,0,,40 or 50 of 'em,\Nlanded right smack\Nin the middle of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.17,0:12:28.05,Default,,0,0,0,,This ﬂuke thing\Nhappened.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.11,0:12:30.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The temperature dropped so fast\Nthat the whole lake froze...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.64,0:12:32.64,Default,,0,0,0,,in three seconds,\Njust like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.71,0:12:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Those poor little ducks.\NDid it kill them?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.08,0:12:38.29,Default,,0,0,0,,No, they ﬂew off\Nand took the lake with 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.35,0:12:41.73,Default,,0,0,0,,To this very day, that lake\Nis somewhere over in Georgia.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.79,0:12:45.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.20,0:12:59.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Come a little closer.\NI wanna give you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.61,0:13:02.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.91,0:13:08.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoop!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.28,0:13:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Come back here, hat. Where\Ndo you think you're gain'?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.92,0:13:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.93,0:13:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I got it.\NHold on, Ruth.\NHold on, little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.43,0:13:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right.\NI got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.30,0:13:36.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here,\Nyou damn hat.\NGot it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.11,0:13:39.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I meant\Nto do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.11,0:13:43.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I... got it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.92,0:13:45.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Ta-da!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.59,0:13:50.13,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.\NDamn!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.19,0:13:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.80,0:14:03.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. Get out.\NGet out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.74,0:14:05.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.74,0:14:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- Buddy!\N- Buddy Threadgoode!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.61,0:14:12.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.38,0:14:14.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.58,0:14:17.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out of there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.05,0:14:22.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.92,0:14:26.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- Come on, Buddy!\N- Buddy'
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.13,0:14:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.26,0:14:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,No-o-o!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.93,0:14:37.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.84,0:14:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy, no!\NNo!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.31,0:14:44.09,Default,,0,0,0,,No! Buddy!\NNo-o-o!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.14,0:14:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,No! Buddy!\NLet me go!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.65,0:14:52.46,Default,,0,0,0,,' No!\N- Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.52,0:14:56.16,Default,,0,0,0,,- You got to go back to the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.22,0:14:58.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NWe're gonna go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.79,0:15:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,- Buddy!\N- You have to be strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.69,0:15:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- It'll be okay.\N- Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.66,0:15:07.61,Default,,0,0,0,,"The Lord is my Shepherd,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.67,0:15:09.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall not want."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.94,0:15:12.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, it like\Nto have killed us all
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.01,0:15:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,But nary a one took it\Nas hard as Idgie,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.78,0:15:24.25,Default,,0,0,0,,everyone thought she 'o' die\Nright along with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.90,0:15:45.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Night alter night,\Nshe stayed by the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.24,0:15:49.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Big George was the only soul\Nshe'd let near her,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.48,0:15:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,and he watched over her\Nnight and day
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.08,0:15:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You know,\Na heart can be broken,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.95,0:15:59.02,Default,,0,0,0,,but it still keeps a-beatin'\Njust the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.08,0:16:01.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Miss Idgie, you'll have\Nto keep this blanket on...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.79,0:16:04.70,Default,,0,0,0,,or you'll catch\Nyour death of cold,\Nyou hear me now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.76,0:16:09.18,Default,,0,0,0,,That's so sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.57,0:16:17.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.24,0:16:19.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you like\None of these?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.31,0:16:21.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, thank ya,\Nhoney.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.37,0:16:23.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.31,0:16:25.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Honey,\Nwe gotta get goin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.54,0:16:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,The Braves' game's\Nfixin' to start...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.01,0:16:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,and you're gonna miss\Nyour... thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.72,0:16:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me.\NThat's my husband, Ed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.52,0:16:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, ma'am.\NHow you doin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.65,0:16:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Um.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.16,0:16:41.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe\NBuddy died.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.29,0:16:43.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Neither could I.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.96,0:16:47.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, well, I enjoyed\Ntalkin' to you, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.43,0:16:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.50,0:16:52.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn...\NEvelyn Couch.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.64,0:16:57.42,Default,,0,0,0,,- I've got to go.\N- You come back and see me,\Nyou hear?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.48,0:17:01.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- Okay.\N- Bye-bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.58,0:17:03.86,Default,,0,0,0,,First of all,\NI want you...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.92,0:17:06.53,Default,,0,0,0,,to truly\Ndedicate yourselves...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.59,0:17:10.63,Default,,0,0,0,,to finding little ways\Nto putting that magic,\Nthat spark...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.69,0:17:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,back into your marriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.96,0:17:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,When we think of\Nromance and marriage,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.96,0:17:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,- what is the first thought\Nthat comes into your mind?\N- Divorce!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.07,0:17:24.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember when counselors\Nused to tell you to wrap\Nyourself in cellophane...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.84,0:17:27.05,Default,,0,0,0,,to put a little charge\Ninto your marriage?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.11,0:17:29.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Do we really pay\Nfor these lectures?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.98,0:17:32.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You can see,\Nit is truly up to you...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.75,0:17:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,to put romance back\Ninto your relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.94,0:18:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn,\Nhave you gone insane?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.98,0:18:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,My God\Npeople can see you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.98,0:18:10.05,Default,,0,0,0,,What if I had been\Nthe paperboy?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.12,0:18:11.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Get in there!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.95,0:18:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you\Nthinking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.55,0:18:18.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.96,0:18:21.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- Evelyn!\N- Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.33,0:18:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, what we really need\Ninstead of this baloney...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.36,0:18:29.43,Default,,0,0,0,,is an assertiveness\Ntraining class for\NSouthern women.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.50,0:18:33.07,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's a contradiction\Nin terms, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.14,0:18:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Especially you, sweetheart.\NYou're livin' in the Dark Ages.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.63,0:19:02.24,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hi, honey.\NI need one of those.\N- Hi!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.30,0:19:05.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm, you smell good too.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.14,0:19:07.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I need one of these.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.24,0:19:10.19,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, this looks good!\N- Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.24,0:19:12.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, indeedy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.35,0:19:24.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.02,0:19:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you come in?\Nand sit down at the table...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.26,0:19:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,- and have dinner with me?\N- I'm sorry.\NThe game's almost over.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.26,0:19:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I just want to see\Na little bit of it.\NWhy you so dressed up?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.17,0:19:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Honey, don't get in the way.\NScoot over a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.81,0:19:43.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.44,0:19:46.44,Default,,0,0,0,,If I'd answered the door\Nwearing only cellophane,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.51,0:19:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,would you still be\Nwatching the baseball game?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.88,0:19:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,No, honey. I'd probably\Nbe checking you into\Na looney bin.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.94,0:20:20.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, sugar.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.25,0:20:22.20,Default,,0,0,0,,- How's my dumplin'?\N- Trick or treat!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.25,0:20:24.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You 're not gonna throw\Nthem hissy-fits, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.25,0:20:27.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Happy Halloween!\NOh, no. No, no, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.55,0:20:29.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You 're meaner\Nthan a damn snake.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.72,0:20:31.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad\Nyou're feeling better.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.79,0:20:35.03,Default,,0,0,0,,- Get back in bed\N- Good thing\Nyour eyesight's failing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.67,0:20:47.81,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey!\N- Mmm. Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.87,0:20:51.28,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey.\N- I was hopin'\Nyou'd be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.34,0:20:55.41,Default,,0,0,0,,My roommate, Mrs. Otis,\Nsaid I could visit her family,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.48,0:20:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,but I said,\N"Thank you kindly,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.48,0:21:00.12,Default,,0,0,0,,but I think I might have\Nmy own visitor."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.19,0:21:02.19,Default,,0,0,0,,And here you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.25,0:21:04.53,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, sit down.\N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.59,0:21:08.13,Default,,0,0,0,,And doughnuts to boot!\NYou can't beat that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.19,0:21:11.03,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, help yourself,\NMrs. Threadgoode.\N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.76,0:21:12.80,Default,,0,0,0,,How's your friend?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.87,0:21:14.87,Default,,0,0,0,,- Mrs. Otis?\N- Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.93,0:21:17.88,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, not so good.\N- Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.94,0:21:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like I won't be\Ngettin' home for quite a while,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.74,0:21:24.19,Default,,0,0,0,,and I sure miss it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.24,0:21:27.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Funny what you miss\Nwhen you're away from home.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.58,0:21:29.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I miss\Nthe smell of coffee...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.05,0:21:32.86,Default,,0,0,0,,and bacon fryin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.92,0:21:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what I wouldn't give for a\Nplate of fried green tomatoes...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.49,0:21:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,like we used to have\Nat the cafe.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.26,0:21:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Ooh!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.20,0:21:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I never told you\Nabout the cafe,\Ndid I?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.33,0:21:51.28,Default,,0,0,0,,No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.34,0:21:55.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, well...\Nnow let me back up a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.01,0:22:01.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, Idgie never\Nquite got over losing Buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.58,0:22:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,She hardly\Never come home.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.72,0:22:09.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Only Big George\Nknew how to find her.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.66,0:22:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,She just didn't seem to care\Nabout anythin' anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.46,0:22:16.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, one summer day
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.30,0:22:20.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll see you,\NGrady Kilgore,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.01,0:22:23.08,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'll\Nraise you twenty.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.14,0:22:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You ain't got nothin'!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.78,0:22:29.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe I do and\Nmaybe I don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.15,0:22:33.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Put your money where\Nyour mouth is, Mr. Sheriff.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.42,0:22:40.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, look what\Nthe cat drug in!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.13,0:22:44.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I came to talk to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.06,0:22:46.44,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna have to wait.\NI'm busy.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.50,0:22:49.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Grady, this\Nis your big chance.\NYou in or out?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.17,0:22:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll make you\Na rich man.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.67,0:22:54.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You just bluffin' again\Nas usual
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.74,0:22:57.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid you're gonna\Nhave to excuse Idgie.\NShe's goin' home for dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.81,0:22:59.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- Say good-bye, Idgie.\N- Where you goin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.05,0:23:04.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where the hell you goin'\Nwith my money?\N- We're goin' home!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.48,0:23:08.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who are you to boss me around?\N- The one holdin' your money!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.49,0:23:10.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Give it back.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.49,0:23:12.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, get in the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.49,0:23:17.73,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.\NI'll get in the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.80,0:23:20.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You win!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.37,0:23:23.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.40,0:23:24.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Sucker!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.04,0:23:27.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll leave when I want!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.14,0:23:30.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know how you can break\Nyour mother's heart like you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.01,0:23:33.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not doin' anything\Nto my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.25,0:23:35.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no? Why do you think\NI'm here for the summer?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.88,0:23:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Your mother was so worried,\Nshe thought I might be able\Nto talk some sense into you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.32,0:23:41.66,Default,,0,0,0,,But you're too busy\Nbeing selfish!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.72,0:23:44.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you\Ntalkin' about?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.76,0:23:48.47,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not the only one\Nwho lost Buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.53,0:23:50.64,Default,,0,0,0,,We all miss him...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.70,0:23:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,but turning your back on\Nyour family is not gonna help.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.94,0:23:58.01,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he got to do\Nwith anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.07,0:24:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I oaks like you 're\Nthe one with the problem\Nforgetting my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.58,0:24:09.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Why just ten miles a way ..
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.15,0:24:11.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Down by the river,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.12,0:24:13.36,Default,,0,0,0,,there lurks\Na den of the devil...
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.42,0:24:17.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Where liquor\Nand gamblin'...
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.32,0:24:20.17,Default,,0,0,0,,and sin abide!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.47,0:24:28.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's turn to page 53\Nin our hymnal.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.84,0:24:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoo-hoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.91,0:24:42.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Big George thought\NI might find you here.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.59,0:24:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,If you give me a chance,\Na chance to get to know you,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.49,0:24:54.23,Default,,0,0,0,,maybe it'll be fun!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.29,0:24:57.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Fun?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.76,0:25:01.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie,just spend\Nsome time with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.10,0:25:03.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Please?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.10,0:25:05.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Suit yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.74,0:25:08.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You sure you don't\Nwanna back out?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.48,0:25:11.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's not too late.\N- I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:11.75,0:25:14.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, hold this.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.08,0:25:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me now,\Nyou like trains?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.85,0:25:22.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes.\N- Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.72,0:25:26.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll get along\Njust fine!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.13,0:25:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, did we\Nluck out tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.50,0:25:36.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Hop in.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:36.80,0:25:39.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Hop?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.41,0:25:42.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh. Give me\Nyour hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.51,0:25:44.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Put your foot\Nup there.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.29,0:25:56.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold that.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.32,0:26:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Ooo-ooo!\NLook at all this!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.73,0:26:08.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you think we should\Nget off the train?\NIt's startin' to move.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.37,0:26:12.18,Default,,0,0,0,,No. The fun\Njust started!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.51,0:26:17.92,Default,,0,0,0,,You all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.98,0:26:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, sometimes I get\Na little dizzy lookin' down.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.28,0:26:24.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't look down.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.86,0:26:41.64,Default,,0,0,0,,- What are you doin'?\N- Come on. Look.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:41.70,0:26:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,They're throwin'\Naway food!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.44,0:26:51.08,Default,,0,0,0,,You talk about\N"give unto others."
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.14,0:26:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, but this food\Nisn't yours to give.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.68,0:27:07.32,Default,,0,0,0,,- More!\N- Give me some.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.64,0:27:36.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, time to get off.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:36.65,0:27:38.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta jump.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.68,0:27:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Lump?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:41.35,0:27:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah jump. The next stop's\Nfive miles down the tracks.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.49,0:27:46.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't wanna walk\Nthat far back.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.56,0:27:49.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you crazy?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.49,0:27:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not kiddin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.93,0:27:55.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.67,0:27:58.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I give up. Jump.-
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.20,0:28:01.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll tell Mama I'm not\Na good influence on you-
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.54,0:28:03.82,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll never jump,\Nwill you?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.84,0:28:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't say "never"\Nto me.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.03,0:28:23.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.67,0:28:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,- You all right?\N- I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.34,0:28:42.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.98,0:28:45.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.18,0:28:47.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Does this hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.59,0:28:50.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.42,0:28:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,- We better get you\Nto a doc-doctor.\N- Shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.79,0:28:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Which way is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:54.96,0:28:58.57,Default,,0,0,0,,About two miles\Ndown the tracks.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.63,0:29:00.87,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.\Nlet's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.67,0:29:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll never be able\Nto carry me that far.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.24,0:29:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.\NNever say never.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.01,0:29:13.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not carryin' you.\NYou're walkin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:19.08,0:29:23.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Julian.\NI owe you one.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.73,0:29:37.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh. Ow.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.74,0:29:41.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Aren't you ready yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.37,0:29:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.54,0:29:48.61,Default,,0,0,0,,This doesn't have anything\Nto do with trains, does it?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.51,0:29:51.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You like honey?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.82,0:29:53.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I like honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.85,0:29:55.85,Default,,0,0,0,,- Fresh honey?\N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.92,0:29:59.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Me too.\NThere it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.52,0:30:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,There what... is?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.79,0:30:07.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll see soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.64,0:30:13.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Now... stay here.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.94,0:30:16.89,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter what happens,\Ndon't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.94,0:30:20.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you\Ngonna do?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.21,0:30:57.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.92,0:31:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Here you are, madam.\NThis is for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.59,0:31:39.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did you do that?\NYou could have been killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:40.02,0:31:43.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.59,0:31:46.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you want\Nthe honey?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.36,0:31:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I got it\Njust for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.77,0:31:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right.\NI do it all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:52.30,0:31:56.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I never get stung,\Nhonest.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.14,0:31:58.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't be\Nmad at me, Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.21,0:32:02.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie.\NI'm not mad at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:02.18,0:32:04.75,Default,,0,0,0,,No foolin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:11.56,0:32:14.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it bad,\Nwhat I did?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:14.32,0:32:16.66,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.73,0:32:18.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought I might\Nbe crazy or somethin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.96,0:32:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.83,0:32:25.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I've heard there were people\Nwho could charm bees.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:25.57,0:32:29.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I've just never\Nseen it done...\Nbefore today.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:31.11,0:32:35.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just a bee charmer,\NIdgie Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.55,0:32:40.02,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what you are,\Na bee charmer.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.08,0:32:42.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, you want\Nto taste it?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.96,0:32:51.70,Default,,0,0,0,,"Satan started to laugh\Nat job's devotion.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:51.76,0:32:57.01,Default,,0,0,0,,"He bet God that job would\Nnever have so much faith...
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.07,0:32:59.18,Default,,0,0,0,,"if he didn't have\Nso many blessings.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:59.24,0:33:03.12,Default,,0,0,0,,"He went on and on\Nso long and so much\Nthat God finally agreed...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.17,0:33:05.88,Default,,0,0,0,,"to let Satan\Nput Job to a test.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.94,0:33:09.08,Default,,0,0,0,,"Suddenly from bein'\Non top of the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.15,0:33:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Job was plunged down\Ninto the deepest pits\Nof misery."
Dialogue: 0,0:33:14.82,0:33:17.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Surprise!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.82,0:33:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie Threadgoode!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.83,0:33:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Tonight we're gonna have\Na real party.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.83,0:33:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Drink this... and then,\Nwe're gonna play some poker.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.13,0:33:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know\Nhow to play poker\Nand I never drink...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.07,0:33:32.07,Default,,0,0,0,,but thank you anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.21,0:33:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Here comes the windup.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.78,0:33:42.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Burn that ball in here.\NBurn 'em in here!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.18,0:33:46.56,Default,,0,0,0,,- Right in the pocket.\N- I don't know how\Nto bat.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:46.62,0:33:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And you don't drink,\Neither.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.49,0:33:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's gonna be a spitter.\N- Hold the bat and swing
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.66,0:33:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Spitter?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.46,0:33:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- She gonna spit at me?\N- She's gonna spit on the ball
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.73,0:34:00.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Swing that bat!\NTake another crack at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.00,0:34:03.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna take\Nanother crack at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.23,0:34:06.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Get 'em in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:13.94,0:34:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Now run, Ruth.\NRun!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.81,0:34:18.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on\Naround the bases!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.88,0:34:20.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't kiss everybody.\NRun!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.95,0:34:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I have never had\Nso much fun...
Dialogue: 0,0:34:24.05,0:34:26.39,Default,,0,0,0,,in my whole life.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.46,0:34:29.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I even got a home run.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.83,0:34:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,A clean one\Nat that!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:32.86,0:34:36.07,Default,,0,0,0,,A straight beats\Nthree of a kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.17,0:34:45.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You know,\Npoker isn't half bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:45.48,0:34:47.65,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your mother\Ngonna say...
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.71,0:34:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,when she sees us both...\Ndrunk?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:51.15,0:34:55.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- You gotta stop worrying\Nabout what people think.\N- I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.12,0:34:57.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You've always done\Nthe right thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:57.19,0:35:00.64,Default,,0,0,0,,You took care of your daddy,\Nthe preacher, when he took sick.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.69,0:35:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You take care of all the kids\Nover at the church school.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.63,0:35:07.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna\Ntake care of your mama.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.43,0:35:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm gonna marry\Nthe man I'm supposed to.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.03,0:35:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You gettin' married?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.37,0:35:17.65,Default,,0,0,0,,As soon as\Nthe summer's over.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.18,0:35:24.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, am I\Ngonna miss you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:24.95,0:35:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,This is\Nthe best birthday...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:28.15,0:35:31.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I ever had.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.67,0:35:47.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth invited Idgie\Nto the weddin',
Dialogue: 0,0:35:50.79,0:35:55.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Mama Jamison,\Nyou put that down.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.13,0:35:57.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my Lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.24,0:36:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,During these next few weeks,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.44,0:36:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,we will be learning to reclaim\Nour own power as women!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:10.85,0:36:12.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Hallelujah!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:13.01,0:36:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And tonight, we're gonna\Nbegin to explore...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:17.85,0:36:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,our own femaleness...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.12,0:36:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,by examining the source\Nof our strength...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.76,0:36:27.14,Default,,0,0,0,,and our separateness.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.20,0:36:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Our vaginas.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.13,0:36:33.94,Default,,0,0,0,,So if ya'll will just\Nslip off your panties...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:34.00,0:36:37.54,Default,,0,0,0,,and straddle your mirrors.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:37.61,0:36:40.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Ms. Couch!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.34,0:36:43.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Ms. Couch!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.85,0:36:48.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, I need to be excused\Nfor a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.28,0:36:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, Missy, could you come\Nwith me to the ladies' room?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:52.42,0:36:56.16,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do you find this threatening?\N- Uh, well, um-
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.22,0:37:00.36,Default,,0,0,0,,- do you have a problem\Nwith your sexuality?\N- No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:00.43,0:37:03.47,Default,,0,0,0,,But I do have a problem\Nwith my girdle.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.22,0:37:31.79,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, fried chicken!\NMy favorite.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.67,0:37:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.87,0:37:42.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.00,0:37:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Those classes I've been taking\Naren't helpin' us one bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:47.58,0:37:50.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go to Florida...
Dialogue: 0,0:37:50.31,0:37:52.65,Default,,0,0,0,,like when\Nwe got married.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.71,0:37:56.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Kyle's gone,\Nbusy with his own life.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:56.12,0:37:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,It'd be\Njust the two of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.19,0:38:01.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, honey, it's just\Nthe two of us here now.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.19,0:38:03.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, you got a good scald\Non that chicken!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:03.96,0:38:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'm tellin' you,\Nthat's really good.\N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:07.03,0:38:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,We could rent a boat...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:09.03,0:38:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,and drift around\Nin the hot sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.77,0:38:14.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you\Nthink about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.94,0:38:17.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just gettin' used to it\Nbeing quiet around here.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.01,0:38:21.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Honey, if those classes\Naren't doin' you any good,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.84,0:38:24.82,Default,,0,0,0,,then don't go to 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:24.88,0:38:27.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone needs a miracle\Nin their life.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.55,0:38:31.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn, game's\Nblacked out!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:39.59,0:38:42.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoo-hoo,\NMrs. Threadgoode?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.26,0:38:45.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey. Evelyn!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.73,0:38:47.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you like it?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:48.00,0:38:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Oooh! Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.44,0:38:54.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- who did it for ya,\Ndarlin'?\N- Believe it or not,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:54.44,0:38:56.39,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a student,\Na little bitty thing,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.44,0:39:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,no bigger than a midget\Nfrom the beauty college.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.11,0:39:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes they come out here\Nand do our hair for free...
Dialogue: 0,0:39:03.52,0:39:06.33,Default,,0,0,0,,just for the practice,\Nyou know.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:06.39,0:39:10.93,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is Ed with ya?\N- No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:10.99,0:39:14.73,Default,,0,0,0,,His aunt said she didn't\Nwant visitors anymore,\Nespecially us.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:14.80,0:39:19.04,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a shame.\NI know he feels bad,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:19.10,0:39:22.10,Default,,0,0,0,,but Lord if he'll\Ntalk to me about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:27.04,0:39:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:29.34,0:39:32.32,Default,,0,0,0,,- Merry Christmas.\N- Merry Christmas.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:33.78,0:39:36.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Threadgoode-
Dialogue: 0,0:39:44.83,0:39:47.54,Default,,0,0,0,,but don't treat me\Nlike you treat your mama.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:47.59,0:39:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,- Grandma!\N- Yes, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:17.19,0:40:19.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi there.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:19.19,0:40:23.10,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes?\N- Uh, is Ruth at home?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.16,0:40:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Who's callin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:25.37,0:40:29.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You just tell her\Nit's the bee charmer\Nfrom Alabama.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:29.74,0:40:32.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.77,0:40:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,there's some bee person\Nhere to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:49.52,0:40:53.16,Default,,0,0,0,,- Idgie.\N- Hi.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:53.23,0:40:56.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You got a real nice home,\Nreal nice things and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.90,0:40:58.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm,\Nthank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:58.97,0:41:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama said to give you\Nthis pie.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:03.50,0:41:06.28,Default,,0,0,0,,So-
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.34,0:41:13.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie Threadgoode,\Nhow are ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:13.41,0:41:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You look so...\Nso grown up.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:18.09,0:41:22.66,Default,,0,0,0,,All the guys\Nmust be wild about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:22.72,0:41:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me,\Ndo you have a fella yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.56,0:41:31.01,Default,,0,0,0,,A... couple.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:31.06,0:41:33.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't decided\Non any.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:33.50,0:41:35.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Grady's the most\Npersistent, but-
Dialogue: 0,0:41:35.50,0:41:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,- Grady Kilgore?\N- Don't say it\Nso loud.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.47,0:41:41.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth, honey\Nwho's down there?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.28,0:41:44.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey-\N- Well-
Dialogue: 0,0:41:44.31,0:41:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- What happened to you?\N- Nothin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:46.85,0:41:48.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothin'!\NWhere'd you get the shiner?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:49.05,0:41:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I-\NWho's down there?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:51.05,0:41:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- You'd better leave now.\N- Did he hit you?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.29,0:41:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did he beat you?\NSomebody's got to talk to him.\N- Idgie.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:58.06,0:42:00.20,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're not\Ngonna do anything.\N- I'm gonna kill him.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:00.26,0:42:02.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna have\Na conversation\Nwith him about...
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.40,0:42:05.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're not gonna\Ndo anything.\N- ...pickin' on\Nsomebody his own size.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:05.23,0:42:07.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not gonna do\Nanything, understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:07.77,0:42:09.98,Default,,0,0,0,,If you care about me,\Nif you really do,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:10.04,0:42:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll turn around\Nand leave this minute.\NYou understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.95,0:42:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, what'd\Nshe want?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.73,0:42:35.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:45.81,0:42:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth's a grown woman,\Nand she knows what's\Nbest for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:50.44,0:42:53.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm, I'm not so sure\Nabout that.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:54.45,0:42:56.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.55,0:42:58.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Grady.\NHi.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:58.92,0:43:02.56,Default,,0,0,0,,- Idgie,will you dance\Nwith me?\N- No.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:02.62,0:43:05.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NIt's only a dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:09.10,0:43:12.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- Miss Idgie Threadgoode...\N- Get your butt\Noff the ﬂoor.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.23,0:43:15.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you dance\Nwith me?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.70,0:43:22.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not dance with you,\Nand I will not marry you.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:22.51,0:43:25.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Go marry Gladys Moats.\NShe just adores you.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:25.75,0:43:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,But she did fall on her\Nhead when she was a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.92,0:43:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just a goofy girl,\NIdgie, a goofy girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.29,0:43:36.29,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who're you callin'\Na goof?\N- Ow-ow-ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.36,0:43:39.53,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who you callin' a goof?\N- Stop that before I get mad\Nand hurt ya.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:39.59,0:43:41.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah.\NYou try it.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.83,0:43:45.37,Default,,0,0,0,,- Grady!\N- There now,\Nyou give up?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.43,0:43:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I'll never\Ngive up!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:47.47,0:43:52.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Grady finally got dizzy\Nand give up.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:52.07,0:43:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Try as they might, none of them\Nfellas could tame Idgie.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.41,0:43:59.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Now,\Na little while later,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.68,0:44:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,a letter\Ncome from Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:08.02,0:44:10.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.\NIt's an obituary.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:10.79,0:44:14.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no, honey,\NRuth's mother died.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:14.29,0:44:16.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.30,0:44:18.41,Default,,0,0,0,,And this\Nis from the Bible.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:18.47,0:44:21.04,Default,,0,0,0,,It's from\Nthe book of Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:21.10,0:44:26.35,Default,,0,0,0,,"And Ruth said,\Nwhither thou goest, I will go;
Dialogue: 0,0:44:26.41,0:44:28.75,Default,,0,0,0,,"where thou lodgest,\NI will lodge;
Dialogue: 0,0:44:28.81,0:44:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,thy people\Nshall be my people."
Dialogue: 0,0:44:50.36,0:44:54.47,Default,,0,0,0,,All right Julian,\Nyou and Big George wait here.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:06.01,0:45:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- Mama died.\N- I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:12.29,0:45:16.20,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm pregnant.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:33.51,0:45:37.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Julian, I got another box here\Nwhen you're done!
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.85,0:45:49.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I never seen anybody\Nwith so many hats.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:49.96,0:45:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't we put\Nthree in one box?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:52.19,0:45:55.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think we can fit\Nall these in the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:55.20,0:45:58.31,Default,,0,0,0,,We're gonna need a separate\Ntruck for all your stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:58.37,0:46:00.32,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell\Nis going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:00.37,0:46:02.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like your wife's\Nleavin' you, mister.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:02.37,0:46:07.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- Sure she is.\NDon't you touch her!\NLet go.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:07.27,0:46:10.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You bastard!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:10.94,0:46:12.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Put her down!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.95,0:46:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,- Bastard!\N- Whoooo!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:15.25,0:46:17.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop it!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.67,0:46:25.08,Default,,0,0,0,,And he's crazy
Dialogue: 0,0:46:25.14,0:46:29.25,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no tellin'\Nwhat he might do.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.03,0:46:53.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on,\Nget outta here.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:03.51,0:47:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:06.22,0:47:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on! Hey hey!\NCome on now!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:09.59,0:47:12.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go. Come on.\NYou okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:12.66,0:47:15.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's get Miss Ruth\Nand get outta here.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:15.33,0:47:19.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Miss Ruth.\NCome on.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.56,0:47:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,If you ever touch her again,\NI'll kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:30.21,0:47:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I sure as hell\Nscared him, didn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:33.51,0:47:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah you sure scared him.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:36.21,0:47:39.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda,\Nthe amazing Amazon woman!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:39.25,0:47:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:41.32,0:47:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda! Towanda!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.02,0:47:49.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn?\NEvelyn!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:50.03,0:47:52.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!\NI'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:52.26,0:47:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I was just lookin'\Nat the pictures, Missy.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:54.40,0:47:57.75,Default,,0,0,0,,They have the greatest\Nstories in that magazine,\Ndon't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:57.80,0:48:00.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Will I see you\Nin group tonight?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.24,0:48:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll be talking about\Nmasturbation.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:02.84,0:48:06.95,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I don't think so.\NI think I've had enough\Nlearnin' for the time bein'.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:07.01,0:48:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\NThank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:10.85,0:48:13.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!\NExcuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:13.65,0:48:16.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Screw you!
Dialogue: 0,0:48:23.39,0:48:25.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me,\Nyoung man.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:25.50,0:48:29.31,Default,,0,0,0,,There was no reason for you\Nto be so rude to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:29.37,0:48:31.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- Get away from me,\Nyou fat cow.\N- What did you call me?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:32.00,0:48:34.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Beat it,\Nyou old bitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:34.57,0:48:37.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you being\Nso mean to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.61,0:48:40.78,Default,,0,0,0,,What did I ever\Ndo to you-
Dialogue: 0,0:48:40.84,0:48:44.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:48:52.66,0:48:55.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at my Stove Top!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:02.20,0:49:05.04,Default,,0,0,0,,BOO!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:05.10,0:49:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, honey, what in the world\Nis the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.77,0:49:12.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:14.28,0:49:17.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:17.71,0:49:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NI need some exercise.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:28.76,0:49:34.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, you tell me what's\Nbotherin' you, sugar.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:34.70,0:49:39.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I just-\NI just feel so useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.34,0:49:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,So-\NSo powerless.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.24,0:49:48.19,Default,,0,0,0,,- Everybody goes\Nthrough that.\N- But I can't stop eatin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:48.25,0:49:53.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Every day I try and try\Nand every day I go off.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:56.22,0:49:59.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I hide candy bars\Nall over the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:59.32,0:50:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,A candy bar ain't\Ngonna hurt ya none.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.36,0:50:06.71,Default,,0,0,0,,One, no.\NBut 10 or 11?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:08.10,0:50:11.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't even look\Nat my own vagina.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:11.54,0:50:15.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't help ya\Non that one.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:15.07,0:50:19.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish I had the courage\Nto get it over with and\Nget really fat.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:23.41,0:50:27.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Mrs. Threadgoode,\NI just-
Dialogue: 0,0:50:27.92,0:50:32.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm too young to be old\Nand I'm too old to be young.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:34.32,0:50:37.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe I'm just\Ngoin' crazy.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.76,0:50:41.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You get hot ﬂashes?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:42.03,0:50:43.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.03,0:50:48.07,Default,,0,0,0,,You get the sweats\Nand your hearts\Nstarts a-poundin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.14,0:50:50.48,Default,,0,0,0,,- How did you know?\N- Simple, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.54,0:50:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're going through\Nthe change.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:54.31,0:50:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I used to burst into tears\Nfor no reason at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:00.48,0:51:02.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You need\Nsome hormones.\NHmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:02.85,0:51:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe some\NStresstabs number 4\Nfor good measure.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:06.52,0:51:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,- Really? Is that all?\N- Sure, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.06,0:51:12.40,Default,,0,0,0,,You get yourself\Nsome hormones.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:12.46,0:51:15.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you get outta\Nthe house and get a job.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:17.33,0:51:19.78,Default,,0,0,0,,With your\Npretty complexion...
Dialogue: 0,0:51:19.84,0:51:23.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll bet you'll be\Ngreat with cosmetics.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:25.01,0:51:28.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I know how\Nyou feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:28.65,0:51:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I was about your age\Nwhen I had my child.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:32.15,0:51:34.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I went through\Nthe change of life.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:34.72,0:51:39.36,Default,,0,0,0,,- I didn't know\Nyou had a child.\N- Yes, I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:39.42,0:51:42.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Albert.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:42.46,0:51:47.07,Default,,0,0,0,,When he was born,\Nthe doctor said it would\Nbe best if I didn't see him.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:47.13,0:51:51.24,Default,,0,0,0,,He said his mind\Nwould never develop\Npast the age of five,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:51.30,0:51:54.28,Default,,0,0,0,,and I should just put him\Nin an institution...
Dialogue: 0,0:51:54.34,0:51:59.02,Default,,0,0,0,,because the burden\Nof raisin' a child like that\Nwould be too great.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:00.21,0:52:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I thought\Nabout Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:06.62,0:52:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,She always said...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:09.02,0:52:12.47,Default,,0,0,0,,there was a separate\NGod for children.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:12.52,0:52:17.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Sol smiled at him and\NI asked for the baby.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:17.49,0:52:22.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, how could anybody think\Nthat sweet, precious baby...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:22.27,0:52:24.51,Default,,0,0,0,,could ever\Nbe a burden?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:24.57,0:52:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, from the minute\Nhe was born, Albert\Nwas the joy of my life,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:28.94,0:52:31.98,Default,,0,0,0,,the Lord's\Ngreatest gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:32.04,0:52:36.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't believe\Nthere was a purer soul\Never lived on this earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:36.68,0:52:39.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I had him with me\Ntill he was 30.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:39.72,0:52:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he went to sleep\Nand didn't wake up.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:45.39,0:52:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes I can't wait to get\Nto heaven to see him again.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.76,0:52:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.76,0:52:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit!\NIt's a boy!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:59.24,0:53:02.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I think a prayer\Nof thanksgivin'\Nwould be in order.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:03.01,0:53:07.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn it to hell,\Nson-of-a-bitch, she did it!\NHere's to Ruth!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:07.08,0:53:11.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie always did have a way\Nwith words around the reverend.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:12.05,0:53:15.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, Ruth had a baby
Dialogue: 0,0:53:15.62,0:53:18.36,Default,,0,0,0,,She named him Buddy-\NBuddy junior.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.42,0:53:23.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Papa went out and borrowed\Nmoney so Ruth and Idgie\Ncould start a cafe,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:23.63,0:53:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,the Whistle Stop 6.22%.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:02.10,0:54:04.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Miss Idgie\Ncan you get the door?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:04.43,0:54:08.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.\NBig George.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:08.10,0:54:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Miss Ruth, me and the missus\Nwant to thank you...
Dialogue: 0,0:54:11.47,0:54:13.64,Default,,0,0,0,,for sendin' that soup\Nover last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:13.71,0:54:17.95,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'll pay you\Nwhen I get ahead.\N- You don't owe me, Ocie.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.01,0:54:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,- Thank you.\N- I'm just glad\Nthey're better.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:20.75,0:54:24.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- How is this,\Nby the way?\N- It's good, very good.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:24.49,0:54:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not happy\Ntill I see clean plates.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:30.63,0:54:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't go on,\NIdgie.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.23,0:54:35.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm talking to you\Nas a friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:35.60,0:54:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,- There's people in this town,\Npaying customers too-\N- There you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:40.14,0:54:43.78,Default,,0,0,0,,But some people\Ndon't like you...
Dialogue: 0,0:54:43.84,0:54:46.01,Default,,0,0,0,,sellin' to coloreds.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:46.08,0:54:48.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Here you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:48.11,0:54:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell you what.\NNext time those\N"some people" come here,
Dialogue: 0,0:54:52.08,0:54:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna ask if they\Ndon't want anybody to know...
Dialogue: 0,0:54:54.58,0:54:56.75,Default,,0,0,0,,who they are\Nunder those sheets...
Dialogue: 0,0:54:56.82,0:55:00.93,Default,,0,0,0,,when they go marchin'\Nin those stupid parades,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:00.99,0:55:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,how come they\Ndon't have sense\Nto change their shoes?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:03.93,0:55:07.28,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hold on there.\N- Y'all ain't foolin' anybody.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:07.33,0:55:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd recognize those size 14\Nclodhoppers you got anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:11.60,0:55:14.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- Just a minute, Idgie.\N- More pie, Grady?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.80,0:55:17.30,Default,,0,0,0,,No, thank you, Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:17.37,0:55:20.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie, I'll talk\Nto the boys.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:21.01,0:55:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,You just keep them\Non out back there, ya hear?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:23.25,0:55:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,- Bye, Ruth.\N- Bye, Grady.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:28.72,0:55:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna\Nget yourself in\Na heap of trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:30.22,0:55:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What, Grady?\NHe's harmless.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:34.29,0:55:38.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You shoulda seen that\Nbig ox down by the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:38.39,0:55:42.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Three solid days,\Ndrunk as a dog,\Ncryin' like a baby...
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.50,0:55:45.28,Default,,0,0,0,,'cause Joe,\Nthat ol' colored man\Nthat raised him, died.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:45.33,0:55:47.28,Default,,0,0,0,,- Remember that, Sipsey?\N- Yes'm.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:47.34,0:55:50.05,Default,,0,0,0,,- He sure ain't' jokin'\Nnow, is he, son?\N- No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:50.11,0:55:52.49,Default,,0,0,0,,He won't even sit\Nin the same room\Nand have a meal today.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.54,0:55:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't make no sense.\NBig ox like Grady won't sit\Nnext to a colored child,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:57.55,0:56:01.00,Default,,0,0,0,,but he eats eggs-\NShoot right out\Nof a chicken's ass.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:25.91,0:56:28.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Smokey,\Nlet's go for a walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:37.55,0:56:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about\Nspillin' my food, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:40.39,0:56:44.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll just\Nhead on.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:52.77,0:56:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,See that piece\Nof land over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:55.87,0:56:58.68,Default,,0,0,0,,See it?\NThat used to be a lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:58.74,0:57:00.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:00.81,0:57:02.76,Default,,0,0,0,,This one November,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:02.81,0:57:04.76,Default,,0,0,0,,all these ducks\Ncome by...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:04.81,0:57:08.09,Default,,0,0,0,,and they landed\Non that lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:08.15,0:57:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Then the temperature\Ndropped so fast, the\Nwhole lake just froze.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:12.32,0:57:15.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Then the ducks\Ntook off and took\Nthe lake with 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:15.42,0:57:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that lake's somewhere\Nin Georgia, the way I hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:18.29,0:57:20.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on now.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.58,0:57:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,God bless you,\Nma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:06.04,0:58:08.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, try this.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:12.08,0:58:16.12,Default,,0,0,0,,- So what do you think?\N- They're okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:16.18,0:58:19.89,Default,,0,0,0,,- The truth.\N- Well-
Dialogue: 0,0:58:22.49,0:58:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,They're terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:25.33,0:58:30.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, well, don't be shy.\NTell me how you feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:30.33,0:58:32.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:45.55,0:58:47.72,Default,,0,0,0,,What'd you go\Nand do that for?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:50.52,0:58:53.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I just thought you needed\Na little coolin' off.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:53.86,0:58:57.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:11.31,0:59:14.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Try these.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:18.55,0:59:21.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I think we need\Nto make a little paste.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:40.30,0:59:43.04,Default,,0,0,0,,What in the name\Nof Christmas are\Nyou two doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:43.10,0:59:45.05,Default,,0,0,0,,She's tryin'\Nto teach me\Nhow to cook.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:45.11,0:59:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at those\Nfried green tomatoes.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:52.08,0:59:56.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You better stop this.\NI'm gonna have to arrest you\Nfor disorderly conduct.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:56.48,0:59:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Arrest us then.\NLet me handle this.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.02,1:00:01.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- All right.\N- Grady.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:03.09,1:00:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha-ha-ha!
Dialogue: 0,1:00:05.66,1:00:09.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Arrest us.\NGo ahead, arrest us.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:09.90,1:00:14.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth, I have to say it.\NI believe Idgie's been\Na bad influence on ya.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:14.34,1:00:17.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I agree.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:56.48,1:00:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be back in a minute.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:59.65,1:01:01.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Y'all keep the show\Ngoing till then.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:01.78,1:01:03.82,Default,,0,0,0,,We ain't goin'\Nnowhere.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:04.95,1:01:08.09,Default,,0,0,0,,- ...down again.\N- She's still poorly.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:08.16,1:01:11.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the baby?\NWho are you?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:14.72,1:01:18.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I ain't scared\Nof you! No, sir!
Dialogue: 0,1:01:18.83,1:01:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,You should be.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:31.97,1:01:34.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Mind your manners, boy!
Dialogue: 0,1:01:43.25,1:01:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Grady,
Dialogue: 0,1:01:45.69,1:01:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,what does Gladys think\Nof you stayin' out late...
Dialogue: 0,1:01:48.99,1:01:53.30,Default,,0,0,0,,and losin' your money to me\Nin poker night after night?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:54.13,1:01:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,She likes it\Njust fine.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:01.53,1:02:04.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- They got Big George.\N- Idgie!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:04.24,1:02:06.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- Let go of him!\N- Let me handle this!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:06.81,1:02:10.69,Default,,0,0,0,,We seen how you treat\Nyour niggers around here\Nand we don't like it.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:10.74,1:02:15.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm the law in these parts.\NI don't care what you\Nlike or don't like.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:15.08,1:02:17.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Turn him loose.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:17.12,1:02:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't get riled up,\Nnigger lover.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:20.39,1:02:24.86,Default,,0,0,0,,You deaf or somethin'?\NI said, let him go!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:24.92,1:02:27.90,Default,,0,0,0,,- Before you get yourselves\Nin a whole lot of trouble!\N- Calm down.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:27.96,1:02:30.74,Default,,0,0,0,,We wanted to have\Na little get-together...
Dialogue: 0,1:02:30.80,1:02:33.78,Default,,0,0,0,,and make sure we see\Neye to eye on some things.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:33.83,1:02:37.28,Default,,0,0,0,,You hear me now?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:37.34,1:02:39.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's let him go, boys.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:39.44,1:02:41.15,Default,,0,0,0,,We've had enough fun\Nfor one night.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:41.21,1:02:43.16,Default,,0,0,0,,- Turn him loose.\N- Come on.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:43.21,1:02:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you're gonna\Nget in trouble.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:47.75,1:02:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now,\Nthat's more like it.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:50.35,1:02:53.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Seems I don't recognize\Nany of you boys.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:53.35,1:02:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Y'all ain't from Whistle Stop,\Nare you?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:58.63,1:03:00.70,Default,,0,0,0,,This ought to do it.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:00.76,1:03:03.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to thank you,\NMiss Idgie.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:03.83,1:03:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Forget it.\NYou'd have done\Nthe same for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:09.07,1:03:12.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Try to get some sleep.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:17.68,1:03:20.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Who the hell\Nwere those assholes?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:20.85,1:03:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,They's just some old boys\Nfrom Georgia come over here\Nto put a scare in you.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:26.19,1:03:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, it worked.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:28.69,1:03:31.40,Default,,0,0,0,,One of 'em was here\Nthe other day for something,
Dialogue: 0,1:03:31.46,1:03:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,seen you sellin' food\Nto coloreds.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:34.06,1:03:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,They decided to come back,\Nshake you up a bit.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:38.20,1:03:41.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I told 'em we don't need\Nanybody from Georgia\Ncomin' over here...
Dialogue: 0,1:03:41.70,1:03:44.24,Default,,0,0,0,,tellin' us what\Nwe can or cannot do.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:44.30,1:03:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,They won't be back.\NI guaran-gol-damn-tee\Nyou that.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:49.54,1:03:52.61,Default,,0,0,0,,One other thing,\Nlittle Miss Smarty-pants,
Dialogue: 0,1:03:52.68,1:03:56.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not wear a size 14 shoe...
Dialogue: 0,1:03:57.02,1:04:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,and I don't\Nmuch care for parades,
Dialogue: 0,1:04:00.65,1:04:04.26,Default,,0,0,0,,bedsheets or otherwise.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:48.83,1:04:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey there!\N- You got to come quick.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:52.23,1:04:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the show\Nhas hardly begun.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:55.47,1:04:58.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You got to come quick now.\NYou hear me?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:00.94,1:05:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- Run, get help!\NRun, quick!\N- Where's the baby?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:03.31,1:05:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:24.76,1:05:30.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, sir.\NI don't believe you\Nshould be goin' anywhere...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:30.37,1:05:32.94,Default,,0,0,0,,with Ruth's baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:17.25,1:06:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he done?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:19.35,1:06:23.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothin' that we know of.\NWe're tryin' to find out\Nwhat's been did to him.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:23.42,1:06:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,He told his hired man he was\Ncomin' to see his wife and baby,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:26.99,1:06:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,but he ain't never\Nshowed up back home.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:31.06,1:06:33.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell, I told him\Nif he showed up in this town,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:33.83,1:06:35.97,Default,,0,0,0,,we'd all have known.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:36.03,1:06:38.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks a little sissified\Nto me.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:38.54,1:06:42.55,Default,,0,0,0,,From what I hear,\Nmost you boys in Georgia...
Dialogue: 0,1:06:42.61,1:06:44.06,Default,,0,0,0,,are a little light\Non your feet
Dialogue: 0,1:06:44.11,1:06:47.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the way\NI heard it.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:47.34,1:06:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Could I interest you\Nin some pie?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:49.55,1:06:53.46,Default,,0,0,0,,No, ma'am, but that\Nbarbecue sure smells good.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:53.52,1:06:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Best damn barbecue\Nin the state of Alabama.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:26.18,1:07:28.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Here you go.\NThat's your 4th one today.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:28.89,1:07:31.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear you're about\Nto eat up all my barbecue.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:31.79,1:07:34.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Sit down.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:34.63,1:07:37.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Sit down.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:45.24,1:07:47.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You sure you ain't\Nnever seen this man, boy?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:47.97,1:07:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir, and I already told ya,\NI ain't never seen him.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:51.68,1:07:54.18,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd do anything for\NMiss Idgie, wouldn't ya, boy?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:56.08,1:07:58.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:01.25,1:08:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Would ya kill for her?\NDid ya kill for her?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:12.23,1:08:14.37,Default,,0,0,0,,No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:14.43,1:08:19.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now, maybe\None of these days\Nyou'll tell the truth.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:21.31,1:08:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Just remember, we hang\Nlyin' niggers in Georgia...
Dialogue: 0,1:08:24.08,1:08:27.06,Default,,0,0,0,,just as fast as\Nthey do in Alabama.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:27.11,1:08:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir, I remember.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:08.45,1:09:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:12.96,1:09:17.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- What are ya\Ndoin' in here?\N- No milk in the house.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:17.96,1:09:20.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Where were you?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:20.13,1:09:23.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Takin' care of business,\Nhavin' a good time.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:25.80,1:09:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been thinkin'\Nmaybe I should move on...
Dialogue: 0,1:09:32.25,1:09:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't believe me.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:34.25,1:09:38.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now, I don't know\Nwhat to believe.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:41.29,1:09:44.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Believe me when I tell ya\NI don't want ya to move out.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:10.19,1:10:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:13.59,1:10:17.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, I've been\Nout here all day.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:44.49,1:10:46.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me.\NI was waiting for that space.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:46.96,1:10:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah? Tough!\N- Face it, lady,\Nwe're younger and faster.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:12.45,1:11:15.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:18.86,1:11:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha-ha-ha-ha!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:21.96,1:11:26.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah!\NWhooo!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:31.24,1:11:33.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:38.58,1:11:41.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:41.45,1:11:44.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoooo!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:47.15,1:11:50.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- Help, someone!\N- What are you doing?\NAre you crazy?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:50.72,1:11:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Face it, girls.\NI'm older, and I\Nhave more insurance.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:04.27,1:12:07.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I never get mad,\NMrs. Threadgoode.\NNever!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:07.97,1:12:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,The way I was raised\Nit was bad manners.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:10.61,1:12:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I got mad\Nand it felt terrific.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:13.85,1:12:17.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I felt like I could beat\Nthe shit outta all those punks!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:17.22,1:12:19.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse my language.\Njust beat 'em to a pulp!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:20.02,1:12:22.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Beat 'em till\Nthey begged for mercy.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:22.22,1:12:24.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda, the avenger!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:26.39,1:12:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll give half the military\Nbudget to people over 65...
Dialogue: 0,1:12:30.03,1:12:32.77,Default,,0,0,0,,and declare wrinkles\Nsexually desirable.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:32.83,1:12:37.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda, righter of wrongs,\Nqueen beyond compare!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:37.54,1:12:40.85,Default,,0,0,0,,How many of them\Nhormones you takin', honey?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:56.32,1:12:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,what I can't\Nunderstand is...
Dialogue: 0,1:12:58.89,1:13:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,how in the hell\Nyou can hit someone...
Dialogue: 0,1:13:02.56,1:13:04.80,Default,,0,0,0,,six times\Nby accident.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:04.86,1:13:07.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Ed, don't make\Nsuch a big deal about it.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:14.31,1:13:18.85,Default,,0,0,0,,- What the hell is this?\N- A low cholesterol meal.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:18.91,1:13:20.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Happy Valentine's.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:24.12,1:13:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,My God!\NAre you tryin' to kill me?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:27.12,1:13:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,If I was gonna kill ya,\NI'd use my hands.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:47.31,1:13:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm worried about\Nmy little friend Evelyn.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:49.98,1:13:52.55,Default,,0,0,0,,She said her husband...
Dialogue: 0,1:13:52.61,1:13:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,will just be watching\Nhis sports on TV...
Dialogue: 0,1:13:54.98,1:13:58.15,Default,,0,0,0,,and she has an urge to hit him\Nin the head with a baseball bat.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:58.22,1:14:01.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell, that\Nseems normal to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:01.15,1:14:03.15,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hi Janeen.\N- Mm-hmm
Dialogue: 0,1:14:03.22,1:14:05.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Threadgoode, would\Nyou like some crudites?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:14.71,1:14:16.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:16.71,1:14:18.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody\Noutta the way.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:18.71,1:14:22.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Give him here.\NLet him go. I've got him.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:24.45,1:14:26.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. You're\Ngonna be all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:26.72,1:14:29.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Open the door!
Dialogue: 0,1:14:29.12,1:14:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Put him in the car.\NIt's all right, honey
Dialogue: 0,1:14:54.42,1:14:56.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I can understand...
Dialogue: 0,1:14:56.38,1:14:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,having a funeral\Nfor an arm.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:58.99,1:15:02.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I just don't know why\Nshe insists on callin'\Nhim "Stump."?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:02.59,1:15:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,She say everybody else gonna\Nbe callin' him that...
Dialogue: 0,1:15:05.66,1:15:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,so we might just as well\Nbe the first.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:09.83,1:15:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, ice cream\Nand cake for everybody.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:14.07,1:15:15.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:20.14,1:15:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,My daddy always used to say\Nthere was a separate God\Nfor children.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:28.02,1:15:31.56,Default,,0,0,0,,The good Lord was watchin'\Nover stump that day.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:31.62,1:15:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,But then it started to rain\Nthat month.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:36.84,1:15:39.84,Default,,0,0,0,,When her husband came back\Nto get her and take her home,
Dialogue: 0,1:15:39.91,1:15:44.55,Default,,0,0,0,,you and your colored man\Nmurdered him in cold blood.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:45.75,1:15:47.35,Default,,0,0,0,,No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:47.42,1:15:52.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, where were you on the\Nnight of September 30, 1933?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:52.76,1:15:55.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I was at the town hall\Ndoing a show.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:55.13,1:15:58.24,Default,,0,0,0,,- And after that?\N- I was at\Nmy mother's house.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:58.30,1:16:00.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah?\NWho was with you?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:00.90,1:16:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- Just Big George and myself\N- What about your mother?\NCan she confirm that?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:05.30,1:16:07.58,Default,,0,0,0,,No, sir.\NShe died a year ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:07.64,1:16:10.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to hear that.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:10.21,1:16:13.92,Default,,0,0,0,,But do you expect 12 intelligent\Nmen to believe you,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:13.98,1:16:16.62,Default,,0,0,0,,although one witness is dead and\Nthe other is a colored man,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:16.68,1:16:20.09,Default,,0,0,0,,known to be a worthless,\Nno-good, lying nigger?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:20.15,1:16:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You expect these men\Nto take your word for it...
Dialogue: 0,1:16:22.49,1:16:25.16,Default,,0,0,0,,just because\Nyou say so?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:25.22,1:16:29.76,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right,\Nyou gump-faced, blown-up,\Nbaboon-assed bastard!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:29.83,1:16:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,One more outburst\Nlike that...
Dialogue: 0,1:16:33.36,1:16:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'll hold you\Nin contempt of court.\NYou understand?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:36.93,1:16:39.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:41.44,1:16:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, Lord.\N- Next witness.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:47.58,1:16:49.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you know that\Nyou were pregnant'...
Dialogue: 0,1:16:53.36,1:16:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,of Idgie Threadgoode\Nand her colored man,\Nknown as Big George,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:57.03,1:17:00.81,Default,,0,0,0,,on the night\Nof September 30, 1933?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:00.87,1:17:02.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir,\NI do.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:02.90,1:17:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,It has been\Nsuggested here...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:05.40,1:17:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,that she and her colored man\Nwere at her mother's house.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:08.94,1:17:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- Can you confirm that?\N- No, sir.\NThat is a lie.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:13.25,1:17:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, shit.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:16.05,1:17:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It has been my habit\Nto write all the dates...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:19.35,1:17:22.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Of the activities of\Nthe church in my Bible.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:22.35,1:17:27.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I show that the night\Nof September 30, 1933...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:27.09,1:17:30.13,Default,,0,0,0,,was the start of our\Nannual revival...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:30.20,1:17:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,down at the\NBaptist campground.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:33.03,1:17:35.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Sister Threadgoode\Nwas there...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:35.20,1:17:39.24,Default,,0,0,0,,along with her hired man,\NGeorge Pullman,
Dialogue: 0,1:17:39.31,1:17:43.45,Default,,0,0,0,,who was in charge of the\Nbarbecue as he has been...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:43.51,1:17:46.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- for the last ten years.\N- Objection.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:46.25,1:17:50.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That doesn't mean anything.\NMurder could've taken place any\Ntime the next couple of clays.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:50.85,1:17:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,- Have you ever been to one\Nof our revivals, sir?\N- Well, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:55.96,1:17:58.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you attend church\Nregularly, sir?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:58.09,1:18:00.30,Default,,0,0,0,,'Course I do.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:00.36,1:18:04.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. Well, maybe if you\Nattended one of our revivals,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:04.96,1:18:07.34,Default,,0,0,0,,you'd know\Nthey last three days...
Dialogue: 0,1:18:07.40,1:18:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,and three nights,\NYour Honor.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:12.00,1:18:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Approach the bench.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:15.04,1:18:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Percy, it don't look like\Nyou got a case at all.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:19.81,1:18:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,In the first place,\Nthere's no body.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:22.45,1:18:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Second, we got us a preacher\Nnobody's gonna dispute.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:34.84,1:18:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,See you in church,\NSister?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:38.65,1:18:40.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Reverend.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:40.95,1:18:45.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe he\Nactually swore on a Bible.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:45.32,1:18:47.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, not really.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:47.32,1:18:49.32,Default,,0,0,0,,If that judge\Nhad looked closer,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:49.39,1:18:52.46,Default,,0,0,0,,he'd have seen it was really\Na copy of Moby Dick.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:54.50,1:18:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,- But why did he do it?\N- For the sheer joy of\Nseeing you in church again...
Dialogue: 0,1:18:58.97,1:19:01.81,Default,,0,0,0,,which I suggested to him\Nmight be your penance.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:01.87,1:19:04.51,Default,,0,0,0,,- You didn't promise him,\Ndid you?\N- Yes, ma'am, I did.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:04.57,1:19:06.52,Default,,0,0,0,,And I never\Nbreak my word.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:06.58,1:19:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,If I live 1,000 years,\NI will never forgive you.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:11.01,1:19:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know what's worse,\Nchurch or jail.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:26.16,1:19:29.30,Default,,0,0,0,,There now.\NDon't you look pretty?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:29.36,1:19:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes, honey.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:31.57,1:19:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll have me\Nlookin' like Ginger Rogers\Nbefore you're done.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:36.31,1:19:40.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't let Mr. Dunaway see me.\NHe's liable to go wild.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:42.04,1:19:45.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad to see\Nyou're in a good mood.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:45.35,1:19:48.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You've slimmed down quite a bit\Nin the last few weeks.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:48.55,1:19:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just so happy Big George\Nand Idgie got off.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:15.64,1:20:18.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn, what in the hell\Nare you doing?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:18.75,1:20:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I need some light\Nand air.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:21.72,1:20:24.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you take\None of your walks\Nor your jog...
Dialogue: 0,1:20:24.99,1:20:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,or whatever it is\Nyou do?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:28.59,1:20:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no dinner\Neither!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:31.56,1:20:36.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed, you have any idea\Nwhy I've been goin'\Nto all these classes?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:36.06,1:20:39.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- No.\N- I've been trying to save\Nour marriage.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:39.67,1:20:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the point\Nof my tryin'...
Dialogue: 0,1:20:41.77,1:20:46.45,Default,,0,0,0,,if you're gonna sit on\Nyour butt drinking beer...
Dialogue: 0,1:20:46.51,1:20:49.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and watching baseball,\Nbasketball, football...
Dialogue: 0,1:20:49.41,1:20:52.55,Default,,0,0,0,,bowling and hockey\Nand golf...
Dialogue: 0,1:20:52.61,1:20:56.49,Default,,0,0,0,,and Challenge\Nof the Gladiators?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:02.19,1:21:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Couch, I'm Sue,\NMrs. Otis' daughter-in-law.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:06.80,1:21:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,How are you?\NI've heard about you\Nfrom Mrs. Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:10.30,1:21:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,She is so sweet. She's been\Nlookin' after my mother-in-law.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:14.07,1:21:16.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, how is\NMrs. Otis doin',\Nby the way?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:16.91,1:21:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Much better, thank you.\NIt takes time getting used\Nto a strange place.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:21.44,1:21:25.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad to hear it.\NMrs. Threadgoode's\Nbeen anxious to get home.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:25.55,1:21:29.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Couch, Mrs. Threadgoode\Ndoesn't have a house anymore.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:29.82,1:21:33.29,Default,,0,0,0,,- They tore\Nthat down.\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:33.35,1:21:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,They had to.\NIt was falling apart,\Nand it was condemned.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:37.66,1:21:40.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:40.66,1:21:44.87,Default,,0,0,0,,- Does she know that?\N- No, well, we didn't see\Nany point in telling her.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:44.93,1:21:47.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It would just break her heart,\Npoor old thing
Dialogue: 0,1:21:47.50,1:21:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,But I am so glad\NI got a chance to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:51.51,1:21:54.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You take care of yourself now.\NBye-bye.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:04.68,1:23:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Evelyn. hey!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:07.05,1:23:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey-
Dialogue: 0,1:23:09.58,1:23:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you like\Nmy roses?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:12.02,1:23:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Since I can't get home\Nto look at my own roses...
Dialogue: 0,1:23:15.42,1:23:17.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I made myself\Na paper garden.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:17.86,1:23:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,- Got everything\Nbut the bugs.\N- They're lovely.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:21.43,1:23:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,- You been here long?\N- Happy birthday!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:24.77,1:23:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh!\N- I shouldn't\Nhave woken you up.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:27.34,1:23:31.62,Default,,0,0,0,,'Course you should've.\NDon't you never let me sleep\Nthrough a visitor's day, honey.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:31.67,1:23:36.42,Default,,0,0,0,,- I look forward to them all week.\N- So do I, Mrs. Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:36.48,1:23:39.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! I can't believe\Nyou remembered.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:39.88,1:23:44.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You made me\Nfried green tomatoes!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:46.52,1:23:48.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm!\NThey're delicious.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:48.62,1:23:51.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's your recipe.\NAre they cold?\N- No.\NThey're just the way...
Dialogue: 0,1:23:52.03,1:23:56.31,Default,,0,0,0,,- we used to have 'em\Nat the Whistle Stop Cafe.\N- Mmm!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:56.36,1:24:00.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You couldn't be sweeter to me\Nif you was my own daughter.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:00.37,1:24:02.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's your napkin.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:02.60,1:24:04.64,Default,,0,0,0,,And wait-wait-wait.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:04.71,1:24:07.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Queen, queen.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:10.45,1:24:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You know,\NI don't feel 83.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:14.65,1:24:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It sorta slipped up on me.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:20.89,1:24:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I never expected\Nto live this long.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:24.39,1:24:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,'Course, the Lord takes us home\Nwhen he wants us.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:39.01,1:24:42.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:42.71,1:24:45.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I was thinking\Nabout Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:45.11,1:24:47.92,Default,,0,0,0,,After the trial\Nwas over,
Dialogue: 0,1:24:47.98,1:24:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything went back\Nto normal...
Dialogue: 0,1:24:50.25,1:24:54.03,Default,,0,0,0,,till that fall\Nwhen Ruth lost her appetite.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:54.09,1:24:56.66,Default,,0,0,0,,By the time Doc Hadley\Nlooked at her,
Dialogue: 0,1:24:56.72,1:25:00.93,Default,,0,0,0,,he said the cancer was so bad\Nshe only had a couple of weeks.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:01.00,1:25:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, we moved her\Nto the Threadgoode house...
Dialogue: 0,1:25:03.80,1:25:08.65,Default,,0,0,0,,and put her downstairs\Nso she'd be more comfortable.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:08.70,1:25:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Sipsey moved in with her\Nand never left her side.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:13.27,1:25:15.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, baby\NI'm right here.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:15.48,1:25:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie just prayed\Nfor a miracle.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:39.43,1:25:42.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:42.97,1:25:45.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Make sure he graduates.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:45.57,1:25:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,And don't... let him\Ncome to the funeral.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:49.84,1:25:52.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't want him going\Nthrough that mess.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:52.58,1:25:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you quit talkin'\Nlike that?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:55.95,1:25:58.45,Default,,0,0,0,,What funeral?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:58.52,1:26:00.90,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna be back on\Nyour feet feelin' just fine...
Dialogue: 0,1:26:00.96,1:26:03.63,Default,,0,0,0,,in just a few days.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:03.69,1:26:06.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Just you wait.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:06.66,1:26:09.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what's the matter,\Nson?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:15.64,1:26:19.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,\Nlet's go for a walk.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:20.01,1:26:21.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you get\Ninto a fight?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:21.68,1:26:24.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I got punched\Nin the nose.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:24.45,1:26:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't play\Nlike everyone else.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:28.02,1:26:31.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I ever tell you the\Nstory about... the oysters?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:31.62,1:26:34.10,Default,,0,0,0,,All the millions of 'em\Njust lying around-
Dialogue: 0,1:26:34.16,1:26:39.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- And God put sand in one of 'em,\Nand it makes a pearl.\N- Oh.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:40.76,1:26:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I ever tell you about\NEva's three-legged dog?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:43.50,1:26:45.61,Default,,0,0,0,,How it never felt sorry\Nfor itself...
Dialogue: 0,1:26:45.67,1:26:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,and howl ought to be\Nsmarter than a dumb dog\Nand not feel sorry for myself.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:51.11,1:26:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You listen to everything\NI say, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:54.51,1:26:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You get real mad at me\Nwhen I don't.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:57.55,1:26:59.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,1:27:01.72,1:27:04.72,Default,,0,0,0,,you know about\Nyour mama.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:04.79,1:27:07.29,Default,,0,0,0,,She's sick.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:07.36,1:27:09.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:10.93,1:27:14.38,Default,,0,0,0,,See, now is the time\Nfor courage.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:14.43,1:27:18.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess you already know\Nthat there are...
Dialogue: 0,1:27:18.20,1:27:21.20,Default,,0,0,0,,angels masqueradin' as people\Nwalkin' around this planet,
Dialogue: 0,1:27:21.27,1:27:24.44,Default,,0,0,0,,and your mom's\Nthe bravest one of those.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:28.71,1:27:30.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.52,1:27:40.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama, I can hit!\NYou should see me.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:40.99,1:27:43.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie, she hit me in\Nthe back with a curveball.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:43.86,1:27:46.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't duck,\Nand I hardly cried.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:46.09,1:27:49.56,Default,,0,0,0,,She hit you?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:49.63,1:27:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, she did that\Nto me once too,
Dialogue: 0,1:27:53.70,1:27:56.48,Default,,0,0,0,,but I think\NI did cry.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:58.37,1:28:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama, I'm sorry\Nif you're sad.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:02.41,1:28:04.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:04.78,1:28:07.89,Default,,0,0,0,,give me a big kiss then,\Nand I'll never be sad again.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:15.42,1:28:18.33,Default,,0,0,0,,And you best not be sad\Nneither.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:18.39,1:28:21.63,Default,,0,0,0,,You understand?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:21.70,1:28:23.65,Default,,0,0,0,,You promise?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:23.70,1:28:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Promise.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:25.80,1:28:29.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Attaboy.\NYou go and wash up.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:53.56,1:28:55.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Sweet baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:59.57,1:29:02.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You two\Nbe alone now.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:03.54,1:29:07.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, girl.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:09.71,1:29:11.78,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:13.71,1:29:16.78,Default,,0,0,0,,That's nice.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:17.79,1:29:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you do one thing\Nfor me?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:21.56,1:29:25.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah, anything.\N- Be good to yourself.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:25.23,1:29:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Even...
Dialogue: 0,1:29:28.23,1:29:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,settle down if\Nyou can find someone...
Dialogue: 0,1:29:30.83,1:29:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,who can beat you\Nin poker.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:41.28,1:29:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,There's so many things\NI want to say to you.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:46.31,1:29:48.85,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:49.68,1:29:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I love your stories.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:52.42,1:29:55.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me a story,\NIdgie.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:58.23,1:30:02.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:02.13,1:30:05.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on,\Nyou old' bee charmer.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:05.30,1:30:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me\Na good tall tale.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:10.37,1:30:14.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me the one\Nabout the lake.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:15.38,1:30:20.02,Default,,0,0,0,,- What lake?\N- The one...\Nthat used to be here.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:22.15,1:30:24.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:26.15,1:30:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that was\Njust a lie.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:29.79,1:30:32.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I know that, fool.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:32.63,1:30:34.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me anyway.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:34.76,1:30:38.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me the story.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:39.73,1:30:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,1:30:45.21,1:30:47.69,Default,,0,0,0,,one time...
Dialogue: 0,1:30:47.74,1:30:50.55,Default,,0,0,0,,there was this lake.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:54.98,1:30:59.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And, uh, it was\Nright outside of town.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:59.42,1:31:04.87,Default,,0,0,0,,We used to go\Nfishin' and swimmin'\Nand canoein' in it.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:04.93,1:31:08.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And see,\None November...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:08.23,1:31:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,this big ﬂock\Nof ducks...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:10.60,1:31:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,came in and landed\Non that lake and, uh,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:15.70,1:31:20.55,Default,,0,0,0,,and then the temperature\Ndropped so fast that the\Nlake just froze right there.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:20.61,1:31:22.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And the, uh,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:22.94,1:31:26.72,Default,,0,0,0,,the ducks, they...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:26.78,1:31:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,ﬂew off, you see,\Nand took that lake with 'em.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:31.02,1:31:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,And, uh.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:34.32,1:31:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Now they say that lake is\Nsomewhere over in Georgia.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:39.39,1:31:42.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you imagine?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:40.15,1:32:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right,\Nhoney.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:43.49,1:32:46.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Let her go.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:46.09,1:32:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Let her go.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:49.53,1:32:53.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You know,\NMiss Ruth was a lady.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:53.83,1:32:57.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And a lady\Nalways knows...
Dialogue: 0,1:32:57.17,1:33:00.17,Default,,0,0,0,,when to leave.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:05.68,1:33:09.79,Default,,0,0,0,,When I think on our\Ndeparted sister, Ruth Jamison,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:09.85,1:33:12.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm reminded of our\NLord's Sermon on the Mount...
Dialogue: 0,1:33:13.02,1:33:15.50,Default,,0,0,0,,and how his teachings-
Dialogue: 0,1:33:15.56,1:33:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It's funny how strong\NRuth affected everyone.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:20.06,1:33:23.47,Default,,0,0,0,,even Smokey Lonesome.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:23.53,1:33:26.20,Default,,0,0,0,,When he died\Na few years back...
Dialogue: 0,1:33:26.27,1:33:28.98,Default,,0,0,0,,he had one possession\Non him,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:29.04,1:33:31.65,Default,,0,0,0,,A picture of Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:33.01,1:33:37.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He was in love with her\Nfrom the first time he saw her.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:37.18,1:33:40.06,Default,,0,0,0,,We all were.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:46.02,1:33:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I shouldn't\Na-told you this.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:50.42,1:33:54.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate death.\NIt scares me so.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:54.46,1:33:57.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Death is nothin'\Nto be afraid of!
Dialogue: 0,1:33:57.06,1:34:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at me. I'm at\Nthe jumpin'-off place,
Dialogue: 0,1:34:00.20,1:34:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,and I ain't afraid\None bit.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:03.50,1:34:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Ninny,\Nyou're so brave.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:08.78,1:34:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth and Idgie were brave,\Nnot me.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:12.78,1:34:16.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be afraid\Nof death if I was you.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:16.22,1:34:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd be more afraid of driving\Nin rush-hour traffic.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:16.37,1:36:19.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, honey.\NLook what I got you.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:19.44,1:36:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah...
Dialogue: 0,1:36:21.54,1:36:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed, how sweet!
Dialogue: 0,1:36:25.08,1:36:27.53,Default,,0,0,0,,- Lilies!\NMy favorite.\N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:27.58,1:36:30.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.\NSometimes I even amaze myself.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:30.78,1:36:34.89,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's the occasion?\N- Oh, honey,\NI just...
Dialogue: 0,1:36:34.96,1:36:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,feel sorry about\Nthe past few months.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:37.99,1:36:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know what\Nyou're really up to and\Nwhat's going on with you,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:42.06,1:36:46.48,Default,,0,0,0,,but I guess I could've been\Nmore helpful with your job\Nand everything, you know.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:47.70,1:36:49.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, why are you...
Dialogue: 0,1:36:49.64,1:36:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,puttin' up this wall\Nwhere you just tore one down?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:52.67,1:36:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...\NI changed my mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:55.88,1:36:58.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't mean to seem\Ndense or anything,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:58.71,1:37:02.95,Default,,0,0,0,,- but what's changed?\N- The air and the light.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:05.32,1:37:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,- Ed-\N- Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:07.99,1:37:10.47,Default,,0,0,0,,You remember how\Nyou used to tell me...
Dialogue: 0,1:37:10.52,1:37:13.26,Default,,0,0,0,,you always wanted\Ntwo women in your house?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:13.33,1:37:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:15.70,1:37:17.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:17.43,1:37:19.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,1:37:19.53,1:37:22.48,Default,,0,0,0,,what if I was\Nthe younger of the two?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:22.54,1:37:26.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't believe\NI get your drift.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:26.14,1:37:30.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I want something\Nmore than I've ever\Nwanted anything before.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:30.74,1:37:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to bring\NMrs. Threadgoode...
Dialogue: 0,1:37:33.58,1:37:35.79,Default,,0,0,0,,to our home.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:35.85,1:37:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I want her\Nto live here with us.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:38.55,1:37:41.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to give her the love\Nshe's given me.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:41.12,1:37:45.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You're kiddin' me, aren't you?\NI'm absolutely serious.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:45.36,1:37:50.21,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I'm puttin' the\Nwall to Kyle's room back up.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:50.26,1:37:53.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, honey, this isn't\Nsomething you're just go and do.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:53.40,1:37:56.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean,\Nshe's an old woman.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:56.14,1:37:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,What if she got sick?\NWho's gonna take care of her?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:59.44,1:38:01.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I will!
Dialogue: 0,1:38:01.21,1:38:03.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't leave her\Nin that place.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:03.28,1:38:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,She's not a stray cat.\NHell, she isn't even family.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:07.25,1:38:10.32,Default,,0,0,0,,- She's family to me.\N- Now, Evelyn.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:11.15,1:38:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:14.29,1:38:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Honey?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:16.22,1:38:18.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, look...
Dialogue: 0,1:38:18.29,1:38:22.53,Default,,0,0,0,,have you mentioned this\Nharebrained idea to her?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:22.60,1:38:25.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- Not yet.\N- Well, good!
Dialogue: 0,1:38:25.73,1:38:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we'll just pretend\Nit never happened.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:28.27,1:38:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm making my own money.\NI'll pay for everything.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:31.37,1:38:34.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't have to do\Na thing.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:35.01,1:38:37.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn...
Dialogue: 0,1:38:37.58,1:38:40.06,Default,,0,0,0,,it's never\Ngonna happen.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:40.11,1:38:42.78,Default,,0,0,0,,So just forget\Nabout it.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:44.38,1:38:47.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you ever\Nsay "never" to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:56.10,1:38:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone helped put a mirror\Nup in front of my face,
Dialogue: 0,1:38:58.97,1:39:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,and I didn't like\Nwhat I saw one bit.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:01.64,1:39:05.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what I did?\NI changed.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:05.54,1:39:09.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And that someone...\Nwas Mrs. Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:09.51,1:39:14.02,Default,,0,0,0,,She needs my love\Nand care, and I'm\Ngonna give it to her.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:15.78,1:39:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,If you'll excuse me,\NI have to go to the gym.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:24.36,1:39:27.40,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you won't listen\Nto reason...
Dialogue: 0,1:39:27.46,1:39:31.10,Default,,0,0,0,,there's always Towanda.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:45.88,1:39:48.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Nin-
Dialogue: 0,1:39:51.52,1:39:54.56,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:54.62,1:39:57.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Those are her things,\NMrs. Threadgoode's things!
Dialogue: 0,1:39:57.42,1:40:00.53,Default,,0,0,0,,- What are you doing in here?\NWhere's Mrs. Threadgoode?\N- Who?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:00.59,1:40:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Threadgoode!\NThe woman who lives here.\NAre you deaf?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:03.50,1:40:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, miss.\NAll they told me...
Dialogue: 0,1:40:06.47,1:40:10.68,Default,,0,0,0,,was that the woman who lived\Nin here died this morning.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:12.54,1:40:14.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh. my God!
Dialogue: 0,1:40:14.74,1:40:19.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Wha- What\Nare you sayin'?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:19.15,1:40:21.32,Default,,0,0,0,,She died early\Nthis morning.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:21.38,1:40:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,They were shorthanded\Nso they asked me to take\Nall this stuff down.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:25.79,1:40:28.29,Default,,0,0,0,,That? all I know.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:47.67,1:40:49.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop that!
Dialogue: 0,1:40:49.68,1:40:52.06,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the matter\Nwith you people?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:52.11,1:40:55.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't you wait a goddamn day,\Nfor Chrissake?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:55.12,1:40:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you have no respect?\NThese are her things!
Dialogue: 0,1:40:58.19,1:41:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, but they told me\Nto get this room ready\Nfor another patient.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:02.42,1:41:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,She may be just\Nanother patient to you,
Dialogue: 0,1:41:05.69,1:41:09.80,Default,,0,0,0,,- but she was my friend,\Nand I loved her.\N- I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:09.86,1:41:11.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just\Nfollowing orders.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:11.87,1:41:14.82,Default,,0,0,0,,- What is going on?\N- Why didn't\Nyou call me?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:14.87,1:41:18.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- You could've called me before\Nyou sent that idiot-\N- I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:18.27,1:41:20.94,Default,,0,0,0,,It never occurred to me\Nthat you would take it\Nthis hard.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:21.01,1:41:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- I didn't even get\Nto tell her good-bye.\N- Oh, I know.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:24.71,1:41:28.68,Default,,0,0,0,,These things are difficult,\Nbut she died peacefully\Nin her sleep.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:28.75,1:41:32.03,Default,,0,0,0,,To tell you the truth,\NI thought you'd be happy\Nfor Mrs. Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:32.09,1:41:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- Happy?\N- Why, yes!\NThis is what she wanted.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:35.19,1:41:37.14,Default,,0,0,0,,What?\NTo be dead?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:37.19,1:41:39.73,Default,,0,0,0,,No, to go home.\NYou just missed her.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:39.79,1:41:42.24,Default,,0,0,0,,She left in a yellow cab\Nabout a half hour ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:42.30,1:41:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't understand.\NWhat? A cab?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:45.07,1:41:49.35,Default,,0,0,0,,She said there wasn't no\Nreason for her to stay now\Nthat Mrs. Otis had died.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:49.40,1:41:52.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs...
Dialogue: 0,1:41:52.11,1:41:54.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Otis is dead?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:54.34,1:41:58.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Mrs. Otis died.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:58.28,1:42:00.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Otis died!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:00.35,1:42:03.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Otis!\NOh, God!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:03.62,1:42:07.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that... I'm glad that\NMrs. Otis died, it's just-
Dialogue: 0,1:42:07.72,1:42:10.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God.\NI've gotta stop her.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:49.80,1:42:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Evelyn,\Nsomebody stole my house.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:53.10,1:42:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It was right here\Nwhen I left.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:56.07,1:43:00.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless- Oh, Evelyn,\Nyou don't reckon\NI'm crazy, do you?
Dialogue: 0,1:43:00.91,1:43:05.12,Default,,0,0,0,,- It was here\Nwhen I left.\N- No, honey,\Nyou're not crazy.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:05.18,1:43:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the place.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:08.02,1:43:12.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would anyone want to\Nsteal an old lady's home?
Dialogue: 0,1:43:12.12,1:43:14.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Wasn't worth nothin'.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:14.32,1:43:17.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, honey,\Nnobody stole it.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:17.79,1:43:21.67,Default,,0,0,0,,They had to tear it down.\NIt was condemned.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:21.73,1:43:23.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.\NI shoulda told you.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:23.93,1:43:27.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, somebody\Nshoulda told me.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:27.27,1:43:32.12,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'm old.\NI'm not a child.\N- I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:32.17,1:43:35.52,Default,,0,0,0,,My husband Cleo and I\Nlived in this house...
Dialogue: 0,1:43:35.58,1:43:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,for more than 40 years.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:38.15,1:43:41.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, it's... it's gone.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:41.62,1:43:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,83 years worth of livin'\Nand all that's left of me...
Dialogue: 0,1:43:45.25,1:43:49.29,Default,,0,0,0,,is what's in this box, a\Nbunch of old cards and pictures.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:49.36,1:43:51.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NI'll take you home.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:51.89,1:43:54.03,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my home!
Dialogue: 0,1:43:54.09,1:43:56.09,Default,,0,0,0,,And now it's gone.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:56.16,1:43:58.70,Default,,0,0,0,,And Mrs. Otis\Nis gone.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:58.77,1:44:00.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,1:44:00.93,1:44:03.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't quite\Nknow what to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:03.60,1:44:07.45,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the first time\NI can remember when I don't\Nhave a soul to look after.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:07.51,1:44:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You can come\Nlook after me and Ed.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:09.94,1:44:12.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you're sweet,
Dialogue: 0,1:44:12.31,1:44:15.12,Default,,0,0,0,,but I think you're doin'\Njust fine on your own.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:15.18,1:44:19.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you know you'd be\Nlike a gift for us?
Dialogue: 0,1:44:19.55,1:44:22.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the reason\NI get up every morning...
Dialogue: 0,1:44:22.79,1:44:26.14,Default,,0,0,0,,and that Mary Kay's\Nhavin' such a good year...
Dialogue: 0,1:44:26.19,1:44:30.76,Default,,0,0,0,,and I don't look like some\Nblob from a horror movie.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:30.83,1:44:34.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,with a little help\Nfrom Idgie and Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:36.44,1:44:38.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. I've got\Nyour room all ready.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:39.04,1:44:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,What does Ed say\Nabout all this?
Dialogue: 0,1:44:41.51,1:44:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll learn\Nto love it.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:48.82,1:44:52.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I ever tell you\Nthat Mrs. Otis was\NSipsey's baby sister?
Dialogue: 0,1:44:53.02,1:44:55.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- No, ma'am.\N- Yes, she was.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:55.76,1:44:59.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Otis was with\NSipsey and me the\Nnight Sipsey died.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:17.93,1:45:21.47,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey there!\N- You got to come quick.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:21.53,1:45:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- The show has hardly begun.\N- You got to come quick.\NYou hear me?
Dialogue: 0,1:45:32.41,1:45:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,- Run, get help!\NRun, quick!\N- Where's the baby?
Dialogue: 0,1:45:35.08,1:45:36.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:55.60,1:45:57.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:57.33,1:46:02.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't believe you\Nshould be goin' anywhere\Nwith Ruth's baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:14.49,1:46:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Like I said,\Nyou ain't goin' nowhere.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:17.29,1:46:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn, you a thickheaded\Nson-of-a-bitch, ain't you?
Dialogue: 0,1:46:24.06,1:46:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you...
Dialogue: 0,1:46:26.10,1:46:30.55,Default,,0,0,0,,you ain't goin' nowheres\Nwith Miss Ruth's baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:36.17,1:46:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, angel.\NCome on.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:38.44,1:46:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, sweetheart.\NIt's all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:42.35,1:46:44.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NIt's all right, baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:47.75,1:46:50.49,Default,,0,0,0,,it was self-defense.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:50.55,1:46:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know why any\Nwhite jury would care\Nwhy I did it.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:55.46,1:46:58.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, I saw it,\Nand I can testify.\N- Excuse me here.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:58.33,1:47:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't mean\Nno offense here,
Dialogue: 0,1:47:00.56,1:47:03.63,Default,,0,0,0,,but I don't know who's less\Nlikely to convince a jury,
Dialogue: 0,1:47:03.70,1:47:05.98,Default,,0,0,0,,my mama...\Nor Mr. Smokey.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:06.04,1:47:08.85,Default,,0,0,0,,No offense taken.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:08.91,1:47:11.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You're a good man,\NMr. Smokey.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:11.38,1:47:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,- You did good.\N- The sun's almost up.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:18.95,1:47:22.33,Default,,0,0,0,,- George?\N- Mm-hmm?
Dialogue: 0,1:47:22.39,1:47:25.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I think...
Dialogue: 0,1:47:25.22,1:47:28.76,Default,,0,0,0,,it's hog-boiling time.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:28.83,1:47:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,No, ma'am. It\Nain't cold enough.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:31.16,1:47:33.94,Default,,0,0,0,,It's hog-boiling time.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:36.87,1:47:38.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Big George?
Dialogue: 0,1:47:38.87,1:47:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- Uh-huh?\N- When is that barbecue\Ngonna be ready?
Dialogue: 0,1:47:42.04,1:47:44.38,Default,,0,0,0,,It's gonna be ready\Nany time now.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:44.44,1:47:49.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Smells so damn good I just\Ncan't wait to get me some.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:49.41,1:47:53.72,Default,,0,0,0,,- Now, don't you forget\Nto call me when that's ready.\N- All right.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:07.46,1:48:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Here you go.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:11.30,1:48:14.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- Miss Idgie?\NSmokey left town.\N- Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,1:48:15.01,1:48:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought it'd be best\Nunder the circumstances.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:19.08,1:48:23.05,Default,,0,0,0,,He asked that\Nyou tell Ruth good-bye.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:23.11,1:48:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Shame he had to go.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:32.56,1:48:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on! I'm comin'.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:42.33,1:48:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- What you want?\N- We want some barbecue.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:45.17,1:48:48.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Not today you don't.\NGo on.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:01.92,1:49:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, this is about the\Nbest barbecue I ever ate!
Dialogue: 0,1:49:06.56,1:49:10.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The secret's\Nin the sauce.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:18.84,1:49:22.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Sipsey?\NMy God!
Dialogue: 0,1:49:28.23,1:49:31.64,Default,,0,0,0,,about what the most\Nimportant thing in life is.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:31.70,1:49:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do you know\Nwhat I think it is?\N- No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:34.10,1:49:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Friends.\NBest friends.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:37.44,1:49:40.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh. Ninny!
Dialogue: 0,1:49:41.64,1:49:43.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Look.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:48.65,1:49:50.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:09.70,1:50:11.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie?
Dialogue: 0,1:50:15.11,1:50:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,- Idgie's alive?\N- Oh, yes!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:19.05,1:50:23.33,Default,,0,0,0,,She's still out and about\NCharmin' bees and selling honey.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:23.38,1:50:27.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes I think\NI catch a glimpse of her.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:33.26,1:50:35.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe we'll\Nsee her today.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:35.76,1:50:38.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:40.07,1:50:42.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:54.28,1:50:58.59,Default,,0,0,0,,After Ruth died and\Nthe railroad stopped runnin',
Dialogue: 0,1:50:58.65,1:51:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,the cafe shut down, and everybody\Njust scattered to the winds.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:03.99,1:51:07.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It was never more than just\Na little knockabout place.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:07.43,1:51:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,But now that\NI look back on it,
Dialogue: 0,1:51:10.30,1:51:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,when that cafe closed...
Dialogue: 0,1:51:12.63,1:51:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,the heart of the town\Njust stopped beating.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:16.80,1:51:19.64,Default,,0,0,0,,It's funny how\Na little place like this...
Dialogue: 0,1:51:19.71,1:51:23.56,Default,,0,0,0,,brought so
